      "dom_id": "question-112129",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "A five gallons water bottle is leaking its content. The number of gallons of water left inside the bottle after $t$ minutes is given by the formula $W(t)=5\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{5})}^{t}.$ How many gallons of water will be inside the bottle after $3$ minutes?",
      "worked_solution": "To get the number of gallons of water inside the bottle after $3$ minutes, we evaluate the function at $t=3.$ Substituting $t=3$ into the function $W(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(3) & =5\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{5})}^{3} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{5}^{3}}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{125} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{125} \\\\  & =0.04.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, after $3$ minutes, there will be $0.04$ gallons of water inside the bottle.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
